1 s; TT 29 / Mastery 232 (EIGHT sets) CORRECT first try with no generalize -- D24 kit mutations (M4A/AAC + FLAC\nunder `.wav`, thin LE-32 Mach-O, PE `0x0266`, ELF `0x0016`/`0x00b7`/`0x00f3`) were all parsed by the D23-generalized\nextractors. Flavor (unasked): \"Windows event logs from several hosts have been duplicated, truncated, and bundled\nwith reports. Count records accurately and find the selectively shortened timeline.\" -> siblings: EventRecordID gaps\n(selective deletion), header-vs-walk disagreement (dirty/truncated), duplicate logs across hosts (Computer), exported\n\"reports\" (CSV/XML) whose count differs from the binary.\nProgression: D19-D22 runnable formats -> D23 APPLICATION DATA -> D24 WINDOWS DFIR LOGS (first structure-WALK field).\nD25-D27 most plausibly the rest of the Windows DFIR block, one artifact per day: registry hive (regf; prebuilt\nregf.py -- header fields, last-written, key counts), prefetch (prebuilt), $MFT / $UsnJrnl (USN = gap), Amcache /\nShimCache (gap), SRUM / ESE (pending gap), jump lists / recycle bin (prebuilt), ETW `.etl` (gap); then PCAP / X.509 /\ndisk images (prebuilt) for D28-D31. A deeper EVTX field (EventID / Computer / TimeCreated / record-id gap) is the\noutside bet if the one-day pattern breaks. Every carried family keeps mutating in the timed kits: keep extractors\ngeneral (multi-chunk EVTX, every codec/container, both byte orders, thin+fat, sorted json lists).\n\n## 1. Atlas\n\n| # | Concept / field | Status | Recognition cues | Standard tool / lib + exact call | D16+ likelihood |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Identity: filename / size / md5 / sha1 / sha256 | seen D1 (+D15 member roster) | any member; id stem names WHICH member | `hashlib.<algo>(b).hexdigest()`; `sha256sum` (I) | high -- every timed kit |\n| 2 | `file.magic_prefix_hex_N` | seen D2 | first N bytes | `xxd -p -l 16` (I); `b[:N].hex()` | high (carry-over) |\n| 3 | `text.utf8_bom_present` (utf16 sibling speculative) | seen D3 | `ef bb bf` / `ff fe`