es java_archive, war, ear, spring_boot). Fields: start_class (`Start-Class`), spring_boot_version, spring_boot_classes / spring_boot_lib (attr values `BOOT-INF/classes/`, `BOOT-INF/lib/`), main_class_is_launcher (`true` iff Main-Class matches `org.springframework.boot.loader(.launch)?.(Jar|War|Properties)Launcher` or another known launcher), effecti\n300:  {\"id\": \"prefixed-zip-launchers\", \"concept\": \"Self-executing / prefixed archives where magic @0 is not PK (shebang jar, exe+jar overlay, SFX, zipapp)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt zip (+ jar, pyz, sfx aliases). Locate the LAST valid EOCD from the tail; archive_start = eocd_offset - cd_size - cd_offset (prefix length) ; fields: prefix_length_bytes, prefix_kind (`shebang` if `#!`, `pe` if `MZ`+PE, `elf`, `script`, else `data`), shebang_line (first line, verbatim, no newline), pe_overlay_offset_hex (pefile-free: last section raw end), overlay_magic_hex_8, embedded_arc\n302:  {\"id\": \"gate-allowlist-dfir-libs\", \"concept\": \"Prebuild gate refuses installed DFIR libs\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS lacks Evtx, regipy, olefile, oletools, dnfile, LnkParse3, lief, cryptography, asn1crypto, dpkt, PIL, sqlite3, wave, ordlookup. Targets evtx-records (python-evtx) and regf-values (regipy) as written will fail the gate exactly like pe-debug-rich-imports did (import ordlookup). Either widen the allowlist (all are in .venv) or rewrite those goals as stdlib/struct parsers. Also `open` is banned: regipy RegistryHive needs a path\n303:  {\"id\": \"python-pyinstaller-zipapp\", \"concept\": \"Python frozen/runnable packages: PyInstaller CArchive TOC, zipapp .pyz, py2exe/Nuitka markers, pyc versions\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt pyinstaller (aliases pyi, python_frozen) on PE/ELF/Mach-O: find cookie `MEI\\\\x0c\\\\x0b\\\\x0a\\\\x0b\\\\x0e` (last occurrence); 2.1+ cookie = magic 8 B, pkg_len u32 BE, toc_offset u32 BE, toc_len u32 BE, pyvers u32 BE (e.g. 311 -> `3.11`), pylib_name 64 B NUL-padded; pkg_start = cookie_end - pkg_len. TOC entries: entry_len u32, data_off u32, cmprsd_len u32, uncmprsd_len u32, cmpr_flag u8,\n305:  {\"id\": \"electron-asar-npm\", \"concept\": \"Node / Electron runnable packages: app.asar archive header, package.json main/bin/scripts\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt asar (alias electron): Chromium Pickle header = u32 LE 4, u32 header_buf_size, u32 pickle payload size, u32 json_len, JSON header {\\\"files\\\": {name: {files:{...}} | {offset: \\\"<decimal str>\\\", size: n, executable?, unpacked?, integrity{algorithm,hash}}}}; file data base = 8 + header_buf_size. Fields: file_names (JSON, depth-first sorted paths), file_count, unpacked_files (JSON), package_name / package_main \n316:  {\"id\": \"ar-static-archives\", \"concept\": \"Unix `ar` archives (.a static libs, universal .a, Windows .lib) members and object architectures\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D20 flavor 'thin and universal binaries mixed with archives'. fmt ar (aliases archive, static_lib, a, lib): magic `!<arch>\\\\n` @0 (also thin `!<thin>\\\\n`); 60-B headers: name[16] date[12] uid[6] gid[6] mode[8 octal] size[10] fmag `` `\\\\n `` ; data padded to even. Names: BSD `#1/<len>` (name follows header, counted in size), GNU `/` = symbol table, `//` = long-name table, `/<off>` reference, trailing `/`\n319:  {\"id\": \"macho-fleet-synthesis\", \"concept\": \"Cross-file architecture-support synthesis over Mach-O / fat / ar / ELF / PE members\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Extend lib.meta.synthesis (fmt synthesis) for ids `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<key>` over the question's `Files: [...]` list (parse like digest_order; get_bytes per set): files_supporting_<arch> / arch_support_files (names whose Mach-O fat_arch/thin cputype, ELF e_machine or PE Machine covers the asked arch: arm64 = Mach-O 0x0100000c / ELF 0x00b7 / PE 0xaa64; x86_64 = 0x01000007 / 0x003e / 0x8664; i386 = 7 / 0x000\n337:  {\"id\": \"archives-tar-7z-iso\", \"concept\": \"TAR / 7z / RAR / ISO9660-UDF headers (archives gap only produced gzip)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt archives were not registered by the earlier `archives` run (tar/7z/rar/iso have 0 fields). Separate modules: tar (ustar_magic, member_names stored order, member_sizes, member_mtimes_utc, member_modes_octal, member_unames/gnames, typeflags) via tarfile.open(fileobj=io.BytesIO(b)); 7z (signature_version `0.4`, next_header_offset/size, start_header_crc32_hex, has_encrypted_header when the next header is kEncodedHeader with AES\n355:  {\"id\": \"regf-values\", \"concept\": \"Registry key/value lookups (Run keys, last-write, counts, UserAssist)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt regf: run_key_values, last_written_utc, subkey_count, value_count, userassist_entries) + value_<path> family, computer_name, timezone_key_name. Use a struct nk/vk/lf/lh/ri walker over hbins (stdlib) since regipy needs a file path and is not allowlisted.\"},\n370:  {\"id\": \"archives\", \"concept\": \"GZIP/TAR/7z/RAR/ISO headers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt gzip) + separate modules tar (member_names, ustar_magic, member_mtimes_utc, member_unames), 7z (signature_version, next_header_offset), rar (version), iso (primary_volume_id, system_id, volume_creation_date, publisher_id). Headers only.\"},\n373:  {\"id\": \"tool-dfir-parsers\", \"concept\": \"Prefetch / MFT / MSG / archive libs\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install dissect.util (LZXpress Huffman for Win10 prefetch), python-registry, extract_msg, py7zr, rarfile, pycdlib, analyzeMFT, windowsprefetch. apt: genisoimage (isoinfo), libscca-utils (sccainfo), osslsigncode.\"},\n383:  {\"id\": \"cpio-payloads\", \"concept\": \"cpio archives (newc/odc/binary) and Apple pbzx payloads\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt cpio (aliases payload, initramfs): newc `070701`/crc `070702` (110-B ASCII-hex header: ino mode uid gid nlink mtime filesize devmajor devminor rdevmajor rdevminor namesize check; name + data 4-byte aligned), odc `070707` (76-B octal), binary `c7 71`/`71 c7` (26-B, endian by magic); stop at `TRAILER!!!`. Fields: format (`newc`/`crc`/`odc`/`bin`), member_names (archive order, `TRAILER!!!` excluded), member_count, member_modes (octal string `01007\n389:  {\"id\": \"eventlog-exports-legacy-evt\", \"concept\": \"Event-log 'reports': Event Viewer CSV/XML/text exports and legacy .evt logs\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D24 flavor 'bundled with reports'. fmt evt (alias legacy_evt): ELF_LOGFILE_HEADER (HeaderSize u32 0x30 @0, `LfLe` @4, major/minor @8/@12 = 1/1, StartOffset @16, EndOffset @20, CurrentRecordNumber @24, OldestRecordNumber @28, MaxSize @32, Flags @36 (1 DIRTY, 2 WRAP, 4 LOGFULL, 8 ARCHIVE), Retention @40, EndHeaderSize @44); records: Length u32 @0, `LfLe` @4, RecordNumber @8, TimeGenerated u32 epoch @12, TimeWritten @","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019BPXbg7cRdMjDthbYAZ6NN","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
