1,'jumplist':1,'regf-values':1}\nfor g in gaps:\n    if g['id'] in prio: g['priority']=prio[g['id']]\nfor g in gaps:\n    if g['id']=='timed-carryover-mutations':\n        g['detail']+=\" D25 (TT 30 / Mastery 270 = 9 sets) all first try with zero generalize: carried extractors held; identity names carry a random `-<6hex>` suffix (ids keep the bare stem), 2 of 9 Mastery sets used a different kit (macos/docx/inner zip, no roster). From D26 the kit carries `d25-registry-001-registry-hive-root-name`: parse root offset @0x24 generally (root not at 0x20, multiple hbins, UTF-16 name when nk flag 0x20 is clear, non-ASCII latin-1 names).\"\n    if g['id']=='synthesis-siblings':\n        g['detail']+=\" D25: still sha256 order over 5 names (note/pdf/elf/lnk/hiv, or note/macos/docx/zip/hiv), per-set lists differ.\"\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"registry-domain-fmt-spellings\",\"concept\":\"GM fmt word `registry` (D25) mirrored onto every regf field with `hive_*` spellings, robust to hive mutations\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"New module lib/meta/prebuilt/registry_fmt.py, fmt registry (aliases hive, reg, windows_registry, ntuser, regf). Import helpers from lib/meta/prebuilt/regf.py (base_block, root_nk, _nk, _values, _subkeys) -- do not change regf.py. Fields: hive_root_name / root_key_name / root_name (root nk name: base block u32 @0x24 + 0x1000 -> cell i32 size -> `nk` sig; name len u16 @nk+0x48, name @nk+0x4c; flag 0x20 -> latin-1 else UTF-16LE; verify flag 0x04 HIVE_ENTRY; if the root cell is bad, scan hbins for the first nk with flag 0x04), hive_file_name / base_block_file_name (UTF-16 @0x30, 64 B, to first NUL), hive_last_written_utc / root_last_written_utc (FILETIME -> ISO `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`, fractional dropped unless non-zero), hive_primary_sequence_number, hive_secondary_sequence_number, hive_sequence_numbers_match (`true`/`false`), hive_version (`1.3` from major/minor @20/@24), hive_file_type (0 primary / 1 log / 6 log new), hive_bins_data_size_bytes, hive_root_subkey_count, hive_root_value_count, hive_root_value_names (sorted compact JSON), hive_root_subkey_names (sorted JSON), hive_checksum_u32_hex (`0x%08x` XOR of the first 508 B dwords) + hive_checksum_valid. Test vectors: D25 hives under challenges/day25/metadata-hive-mind/solver/cases/*/artifacts (root names and base-block names differ in every one).\"},\n {\"id\":\"registry-hive-identity-values\",\"concept\":\"Hive identity and host labels: hive type, root values (Marker/Ordinal), ComputerName, machine/user SID, OS product -- D25 flavor 'separated from host labels'\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt registry (aliases regf, hive). Value walk: nk value count @+0x24, value list off @+0x28 -> u32 offsets -> `vk` cells: name len u16 @+2, data size u32 @+4 (bit 31 = inline in the offset field), data off @+8, type u32 @+0xc, flags u16 @+0x10 (1 = ASCII name), name @+0x14; big data `db` when size > 16344. Type names REG_NONE/SZ/EXPAND_SZ/BINARY/DWORD/DWORD_BIG_ENDIAN/LINK/MULTI_SZ/QWORD. Fields: root_value_<name> (data verbatim: REG_SZ to first NUL, DWORD/QWORD base-10, BINARY lowercase hex, MULTI_SZ JSON list), root_value_types (JSON sorted `name:REG_*`), value_<path> generic (path relative to root, `\\\\` separated, case-insensitive match), hive_type (`SYSTEM` if ControlSet00N + Select, `SOFTWARE` if Microsoft + Classes, `SAM` if SAM\\\\Domains, `SECURITY` if Policy, `NTUSER` if Software + Environment/Console, `USRCLASS` if Local Settings or root ends `_Classes`, `AMCACHE` if Root\\\\InventoryApplicationFile, `BCD` if Objects + Description, `DEFAULT`), computer_name (SYSTEM Select\\\\Current -> ControlSet00N\\\\Control\\\\ComputerName\\\\ComputerName\\\\ComputerName), product_name / install_date_utc / registered_owner (SOFTWARE Microsoft\\\\Windows NT\\\\CurrentVersion), machine_sid (SAM Domains\\\\Account V last 12 B -> S-1-5-21-a-b-c), timezone_key_name. D25 hives: root values `Marker` REG_SZ (`HUNTRESS-HIVE-4203` single; random hex timed) + `Ordinal` REG_DWORD inline (4203 = marker number).\"},\n {\"id\":\"registry-planted-hive-synthesis\",\"concept\":\"Cross-hive synthesis: regroup hives by host, isolate the planted / odd hive\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Extend lib/meta/prebuilt/synthesis_*.py with a registry module over the question's `Files: [...]` (or every regf member of the container; get_bytes per set). Fields (ids `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<key>`): host_groups (members grouped by the same Marker/host value or ComputerName/machine SID -> sorted JSON of sorted name lists), planted_hive / odd_one_out (the member whose root name does not match its group, whose base-block FileName/root disagree while others agree, whose last-written is outside its group's range, whose seq1 != seq2, whose checksum is invalid, or whose version/type differs -- report the single member when exactly one differs, else `none`), order_by_last_written (names ascending), root_names_by_member (JSON object name->root). Spelling: names verbatim, compact JSON, sorted unless the key says order.\"},\n {\"id\":\"crash-memory-dump-headers\",\"concept\":\"Windows crash/memory dumps: minidump MDMP, kernel PAGEDU64/PAGEDUMP, hiberfil -- next Windows DFIR artifact\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt minidump (aliases mdmp, dmp, crashdump, dump): header `MDMP` @0 + version u16 0xa793 @4, implementation u16 @6, NumberOfStreams u32 @8, StreamDirectoryRva u32 @12, CheckSum u32 @16, TimeDateStamp u32 @20 (unix -> ISO Z), Flags u64 @24 (emit `0x%016x`). Directory entries 12 B {StreamType u32, DataSize u32, Rva u32}; stream_types (JSON list of ints in directory order + names ThreadListStream 3, ModuleListStream 4, MemoryListStream 5, ExceptionStream 6, SystemInfoStream 7, Memory64ListStream 9, HandleDataStream 12, MiscInfoStream 15, ThreadInfoListStream 17). SystemInfo: ProcessorArchitecture u16 (0 x86 `0x0000`, 5 ARM, 9 AMD64, 12 ARM64), NumberOfProcessors u8 @+6, ProductType @+7, Major/Minor/Build @+8/+12/+16, CSDVersionRva -> MINIDUMP_STRING (u32 len + UTF-16). ModuleList: count u32 then 108-B MINIDUMP_MODULE {BaseOfImage u64, SizeOfImage u32, CheckSum, TimeDateStamp, ModuleNameRva ...} -> module_names (path verbatim, file order) + main_module (first). Exception stream: exception_code_u32_hex, exception_address. fmt kernel_dump (aliases crashdump, memory_dump): `PAGEDU64` (64-bit; MachineImageType u32 @0x30, NumberProcessors @0x34, BugCheckCode @0x38 hex, BugCheckParameters u64 x4 @0x40, DumpType u32 @0xf98, SystemTime FILETIME @0xfa8) / `PAGEDUMP` (32-bit offsets @0x20/0x24/0x28...). fmt hiberfil: magic `hibr`/`HIBR`/`wake`/`RSTR`/zeroed @0 -> state word.\"},\n {\"id\":\"thumbcache-rdp-cache\",\"concept\":\"Explorer thumbcache / iconcache and RDP bitmap cache files\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt thumbcache (aliases thumbcache_db, iconcache): header `CMMM` @0, format version u32 @4 (20 Vista, 21 Win7, 30 Win8, 31 Win8.1, 32 Win10), cache type u32 @8 (16/32/48/96/256/768/1280/1920/2560/sr/wide/exif/idx -- emit raw int + size label), first entry offset / available-entry offset (offsets depend on version). Entries `CMMM` @0 {size u32, entry hash u64, ext/name len, padding, data size, header checksum u64, data checksum u64; Win7 has UTF-16 extension}; fields entry_count, entry_hashes (`0x%016x` file order), data_magic set (`ff d8`/`89 50`/`42 4d`). thumbcache_idx.db `IMMM`. fmt rdp_cache (alias bmc, bcache): Cache0000.bin `RDP8bmp\\\\0` @0 + version u32 @8, tiles {key u64, width u16, height u16, 64x64x4 BGRA} -> tile_count, tile_dimensions set; bcache2/22/24.bmc legacy (no header, 0x14-B tile header).\"},\n {\"id\":\"timeline-bits-wmi-persistence\",\"concept\":\"Windows Timeline ActivitiesCache.db, BITS jobs, WMI repository persistence (OBJECTS.DATA)\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt timeline (alias activitiescache): SQLite Activity table (stdlib b-tree walk via lib/meta/prebuilt/sqlite.py helpers): AppId JSON -> application names, ActivityType counts, StartTime/EndTime epoch -> ISO Z, Payload displayText. fmt bits (aliases qmgr): legacy qmgr0.dat/qmgr1.dat job header GUID `28 32 ed 09 a6 c7 e9 45` ... job name / URL / local path UTF-16 strings (regex carve, file order); Win10 qmgr.db is ESE (reuse ese.py header). fmt wmi (aliases objects_data, cim): regex over UTF-16 and ASCII for `CommandLineEventConsumer`, `ActiveScriptEventConsumer`, `__EventFilter`, `__FilterToConsumerBinding`; consumer_names, filter_queries (WQL `SELECT ...`), command_line_templates (verbatim), sorted JSON.\"},\n]\nfor g in new: assert g['id'] not in ids, g['id']\n# insert new prio-1 after the ese gap, prio 2/3 near the end of their priority groups\nout=[]\nfor g in gaps:\n    out.append(g)\n    if g['id']=='usn-journal-records':\n        out += [new[0], new[3]]\n    if g['id']=='customdestinations-ms':\n        out += [new[1], new[2], new[4]]\nout.append(new[5])\n# order by priority (stable)\nout.sort(key=lambda g:g['priority'])\nassert len(out)==len(gaps)+6\nbody=\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in out)\nt=t[:m.start(2)]+body+t[m.end(2):]\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\nPYEOF\n.venv/bin/python -I $TMPDIR/d25tl/edit_atlas.py && echo ok","description":"Apply day25 edits to coverage atlas"}}}
